{"kind":"request","text":"codex: cut the routine commitment loop down to what the log shows is doing work. Two cuts, and deliberately no further:\n\n1. Artifact-as-report. An artifact statement that rests on the promise and names the exact implementation head discharges the report obligation. No separate ready-for-review report record; the artifact already carries the head, the basis, and the conditions met.\n2. Merge-as-ratification. The merge of an approved exact head stands as the requester's ratification of the fulfilment and closes the commitment. No separate ratify act after the merge. You have design latitude on whether the merge also stands as ratification of the review approval it merges or whether that ratification remains an explicit act before the merge gate — pick the reading that keeps the merge gate's authority story sound, and record which you chose and why.\n\nOUT OF SCOPE, deliberately: the independent review itself, the reviewer's verdict record, and the different-agent rule all stay exactly as they are. This cuts ceremony, not scrutiny. A request that resolves without a merge — withdrawn, refused, abandoned — still closes through an explicit report or supersession.\n\nWHY, measured at depth 4651 (180 merges on main, log spanning 2026-08-06 to 2026-08-12): the loop costs ~26 durable records per merge; 537 ratify acts have been filed; and 286 of 796 commitments (36%) never closed with a report. A closing half that is skipped a third of the time is bookkeeping, not coordination. The ratified self-initiated-work exception already established the principle that a loop keeps no promise the log does not need; this extends the same economy to the closing half of assigned work, where the merge itself is the requester's acceptance in every workflow that has ever worked.","body":{"conditions":"The fold treats a conforming artifact statement (resting on the promise, naming the exact head) as discharging the report obligation, pinned by tests. The fold treats the merge of an approved exact head as closing the requester's ratification obligation on that commitment, pinned by tests. The chosen reading for review-approval ratification is recorded in the head and reflected in the merge gate's tests. A commitment that resolves without a merge still closes through an explicit report or supersession, with a test. docs/concepts/work-loop.md and its state diagram are updated in the same head. AGENTS.md is not rewritten under this request; that work is filed separately and rests on this one.","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}